From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:32:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dashboard): leave the model settings a deployment sets
 alone

A deployment can pin the main model and custom endpoints in the managed scope and supply provider keys in the process environment. The dashboard's setup routes only knew config.yaml and .env: setting the default answered ok while the pinned one stayed (and wrote model.base_url and model.api_mode next to it), a removed managed endpoint came back on the next start, and a key saved over one from the environment went to .env, which loads with override and hid the deployment's key for good. dashboard.managed_read_only (false = off) marks these items (managed on endpoints and on the default in the custom-endpoints list and /api/model/info, managed or in_environment on /api/env rows, never the value) and refuses their writes with 409 and where they are set. Setting the default also stops writing base_url and api_mode for a provider that is not a custom endpoint.
---
